course: dictionary
lesson: 9332
title: Spinach, a leafy green
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Spinach is a dark green leafy vegetable. You can eat it raw in a salad or cooked in a hot dish. When you meet a word you do not know, look at the words around it, because they are its context. «Carrots and beetroot are roots, celery and asparagus are stems, lettuce and spinach are leaves» tells you that spinach is a leaf.
explain: Spinach is good for you. It has vitamins A, C and K, folate and iron. Health lessons often talk about it, and you will see it in phrases like «spinach leaves» and «spinach and ricotta».
explain: Context can also warn you about a story that is not true. «Spinach is healthy, but it gives no sudden muscles.» Popeye is a cartoon that eats spinach to get strong, but the sentence tells you that muscles grow slowly, with exercise, food and rest. Always ask: does this fit real life?
fact: Spinach is a dark green leafy vegetable that can be eaten raw in salads or cooked.
fact: Spinach has vitamins A, C and K, folate and iron.
fact: Spinach shrinks a lot when it is cooked, so you need a big pile of raw leaves to make a small portion.
fact: «Spinach is not as iron-rich as the old story says.» Meat, beans and lentils are also good sources of iron.
fact: Popeye the Sailor is a cartoon. In real life, muscles grow over months with exercise, food and rest, not from one can of spinach.
exercise: «Carrots and beetroot are roots, celery and asparagus are stems, lettuce and spinach are leaves.» Which group is spinach in? | Roots | Flowers | Stems | *Leaves
exercise: Popeye eats a can of spinach to get super strong. Why is this not true to life? | *Muscles grow over months, with exercise, food and rest | Spinach is a root, so it works slowly | Spinach gives you big muscles in one minute
exercise: What happens to spinach when you cook it? | It turns blue | *It shrinks a lot | It gets bigger | It stays exactly the same size
test: «No single food has everything, so eating only pasta like Jade in Belfast misses whole groups.» Why does Jade miss out if she eats only pasta? | Pasta has every vitamin in it | *Pasta does not have everything, so whole food groups are missed | Pasta is a leafy green vegetable
test: «The famous story that spinach's iron was overrated because of a misplaced decimal point is itself disputed and partly a myth.» What does disputed mean here? | Cooked for too long | Proven and agreed by everyone | Hidden under the leaves | *Argued about, and not agreed on
exam: Which statement about spinach is true? | Spinach gives you super strength in one day | *Spinach is a dark green leafy vegetable that can be eaten raw or cooked | Spinach is a fruit that grows on trees | Spinach has no vitamins at all
